{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "heat_1d_varcoeff_zero_flux",
    "description": "MMS driver: 1-D VARIABLE-COEFFICIENT heat equation u_t = div(k(x) grad u) + S(x,t) on the unit interval [0, 1] with zero-flux (homogeneous Neumann) boundaries, discretized by the conservative finite-volume rule grids/cartesian_uniform_1d/rules/varcoeff_laplacian_zero_flux_bc. The consumer writes the operator as the conservative compound D(k*D(u,x),x) (coefficient on the LEFT), which that rule matches at priority 10 and lowers to the arithmetic-mean flux-difference stencil. The coefficient k(x) = 1 + 0.5 cos(2 pi x) is a consumer-supplied observed of shape [x] (positive on [0,1], range [0.5,1.5]); it is read by the rule body at the faces via kf[i+1/2]=(k[i]+k[i+1])/2. Manufactured solution u(x,t) = exp(-pi^2 t) cos(pi x): cos(pi x) has zero gradient at x=0 and x=1, so the physical flux k u_x vanishes at both walls and matches the zero-flux closure. Because cos(pi x) is NOT an eigenfunction of the variable-coefficient operator, a forcing term S(x,t) = u_t - div(k grad u) is added so u is exact for the continuous PDE. With this u and k, div(k grad u) = exp(-pi^2 t)[-pi k'(x) sin(pi x) - pi^2 k(x) cos(pi x)] and u_t = -pi^2 exp(-pi^2 t) cos(pi x); the algebra (product-to-sum with k'=-pi sin 2pi x) collapses to the closed form S(x,t) = exp(-pi^2 t) * 0.25 pi^2 (3 cos(3 pi x) - cos(pi x)), spelled below as a time factor exp(-pi^2 t) times an aggregate over cell centers. The grid's consumer-supplied geometry contract (grids/cartesian_uniform_1d/grid.esm) is fulfilled for [0,1]: x0 = 0 (parameter) and dx = 1/N (an observed dividing by the metaparameter name N, substituted at load per esm-spec 9.7.6, so the convergence sweep's loader-API rebinding of N keeps dx consistent) resolve the rule body's free dx at evaluation. Initial condition, coefficient, forcing, and test references all spell the cell-center coordinate x_i = (i - 1/2)/N inline with load-foldable scalars (0 + (i - 1/2)(1/N)) rather than invoking the free-name x_coord template: the official 6.6.5/ic build-time cellwise evaluation is scope-free (model parameters/observeds are not in scope there), and spelling k and S the same way keeps them algebraically identical to what the runtime rule reads. The SAME rule also serves the nonlinear case (a consumer declaring k as an observed k=f(u)); this driver exercises the variable-coefficient dual.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "esd:problem",
      "grid:cartesian_uniform_1d",
      "equation:heat",
      "mms"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Roache, P. J. (2002). Code verification by the method of manufactured solutions. J. Fluids Eng. 124(1), 4-10.",
        "doi": "10.1115/1.1436090"
      },
      {
        "citation": "LeVeque, R. J. (2007). Finite Difference Methods for Ordinary and Partial Differential Equations. SIAM. Section 2.15 (variable-coefficient conservative form)."
      }
    ]
  },
  "models": {
    "Heat": {
      "expression_template_imports": [
        {
          "ref": "../grids/cartesian_uniform_1d/rules/varcoeff_laplacian_zero_flux_bc.esm"
        }
      ],
      "variables": {
        "u": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "K",
          "shape": [
            "x"
          ],
          "description": "Temperature field over the x index set."
        },
        "x0": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "m",
          "default": 0,
          "description": "Left domain edge a = 0 (unit interval): the grid's x0 free name (consumer-supplied geometry contract, grids/cartesian_uniform_1d/grid.esm)."
        },
        "dx": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m",
          "description": "Grid spacing (b - a)/N = 1/N: the grid's dx free name, resolved inside the rewrite rule's expanded body at evaluation. N is the document-scoped metaparameter (re-exported up the import chain), substituted as an integer literal at load (esm-spec 9.7.6), so loader-API rebinding for the convergence sweep keeps dx consistent."
        },
        "k": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m^2/s",
          "shape": [
            "x"
          ],
          "description": "Variable conductivity k(x) = 1 + 0.5 cos(2 pi x) over the x index set, evaluated at cell centers x_gi = (gi - 1/2)/N (spelled inline from literals and the metaparameter name N). Positive on [0,1] (range [0.5,1.5]). Bound by the rule's match as the coefficient k (the left factor of k*D(u,x)) and read by the expanded stencil at the faces via kf[i+1/2]=(k[i]+k[i+1])/2. k has zero gradient at both walls, consistent with the zero-flux closure. The aggregate loops over `gi`, NOT the stencil's interior index `i`: an array coefficient authored as an aggregate observed is inlined into the stencil's [2,N-1] aggregate at evaluation, and a shared loop-index name would be captured — so, exactly as the nonuniform grid's geometry observeds xc/dxw loop over `gi`, a consumer-supplied coefficient field must loop over an index distinct from `i` (see the rule's description)."
        }
      },
